//@version=6
// All Candlestick Patterns Library
// Description: A comprehensive Pine Script library for detecting candlestick patterns.
//              The library provides functions to calculate candlestick properties, detect trends,
//              and identify various bullish and bearish candlestick patterns. It is designed for
//              reusability in TradingView scripts, allowing users to integrate pattern detection
//              into their own indicators or strategies.
library("AllCandlestickPatternsLibrary", overlay = true)

// SECTION 1: TREND DETECTION
// This section contains functions to determine the market trend based on user-defined rules,
// such as SMA50 or a combination of SMA50 and SMA200. These functions are used to contextualize
// pattern detection, as many patterns depend on whether the market is in an uptrend or downtrend.

// Detects the market trend based on the specified rule.
// @param downTrend Initial downtrend condition.
// @param upTrend Initial uptrend condition.
// @param trendRule The rule for trend detection ("SMA50" or "SMA50, SMA200").
// @param p_close Current closing price.
// @param sma50 Simple Moving Average over 50 periods.
// @param sma200 Simple Moving Average over 200 periods.
// @returns A tuple of [bool downTrend, bool upTrend].
export detectTrend(bool downTrend, bool upTrend, string trendRule, float p_close, float sma50, float sma200) =>
    var bool C_DownTrend = downTrend
    var bool C_UpTrend = upTrend
    if trendRule == "SMA50"
        priceAvg = sma50
        C_DownTrend := p_close < priceAvg
        C_UpTrend := p_close > priceAvg
    else if trendRule == "SMA50, SMA200"
        C_DownTrend := p_close < sma50 and sma50 < sma200
        C_UpTrend := p_close > sma50 and sma50 > sma200
    [C_DownTrend, C_UpTrend]

// SECTION 2: CANDLESTICK PROPERTY CALCULATIONS
// This section contains a function to calculate core properties of a candlestick, such as body size,
// shadow lengths, and whether it is a doji. These properties are used by pattern detection functions
// to identify specific candlestick formations.

// Calculates properties of a candlestick based on OHLC data and configuration parameters.
// @param p_open Candlestick open price.
// @param p_close Candlestick close price.
// @param p_high Candlestick high price.
// @param p_low Candlestick low price.
// @param bodyAvg Average body size (e.g., from EMA of body sizes).
// @param shadowPercent Minimum shadow size as a percentage of body size.
// @param shadowEqualsPercent Tolerance for equal shadows in doji detection.
// @param dojiBodyPercent Maximum body size as a percentage of range for doji.
// @returns A tuple of calculated properties: [bodyHi, bodyLo, body, smallBody, longBody, upShadow,
//          dnShadow, hasUpShadow, hasDnShadow, whiteBody, blackBody, candleRange, isInsideBar,
//          bodyMiddle, shadowEquals, isDojiBody, doji].
export calculateCandleProperties(float p_open, float p_close, float p_high, float p_low, float bodyAvg, float shadowPercent, float shadowEqualsPercent, float dojiBodyPercent) =>
    C_BodyHi = math.max(p_close, p_open)
    C_BodyLo = math.min(p_close, p_open)
    C_Body = C_BodyHi - C_BodyLo
    C_SmallBody = C_Body < bodyAvg
    C_LongBody = C_Body > bodyAvg
    C_UpShadow = p_high - C_BodyHi
    C_DnShadow = C_BodyLo - p_low
    C_HasUpShadow = C_UpShadow > shadowPercent / 100 * C_Body
    C_HasDnShadow = C_DnShadow > shadowPercent / 100 * C_Body
    C_WhiteBody = p_open < p_close
    C_BlackBody = p_open > p_close
    C_Range = p_high - p_low
    C_IsInsideBar = C_BodyHi[1] > C_BodyHi and C_BodyLo[1] < C_BodyLo
    C_BodyMiddle = C_Body / 2 + C_BodyLo
    C_ShadowEquals = C_UpShadow == C_DnShadow or (math.abs(C_UpShadow - C_DnShadow) / C_DnShadow * 100) < shadowEqualsPercent and (math.abs(C_DnShadow - C_UpShadow) / C_UpShadow * 100) < shadowEqualsPercent
    C_IsDojiBody = C_Range > 0 and C_Body <= C_Range * dojiBodyPercent / 100
    C_Doji = C_IsDojiBody and C_ShadowEquals
    [C_BodyHi, C_BodyLo, C_Body, C_SmallBody, C_LongBody, C_UpShadow, C_DnShadow, C_HasUpShadow, C_HasDnShadow, C_WhiteBody, C_BlackBody, C_Range, C_IsInsideBar, C_BodyMiddle, C_ShadowEquals, C_IsDojiBody, C_Doji]

// SECTION 3: CANDLESTICK PATTERN DETECTION
// This section contains functions to detect specific candlestick patterns. Each function evaluates
// whether a pattern is present based on candlestick properties and trend conditions, returning a
// tuple with the detection result, pattern name, type (Bullish/Bearish), and a description for use
// in tooltips or alerts.

// Pattern: On Neck (Bearish)
// Detects the On Neck Bearish pattern.
// @param downTrend Current downtrend condition.
// @param blackBody Whether the candle has a black body.
// @param longBody Whether the candle has a long body.
// @param whiteBody Whether the candle has a white body.
// @param p_open Candlestick open price.
// @param p_close Candlestick close price.
// @param p_low Candlestick low price.
// @param bodyAvg Average body size.
// @param smallBody Whether the candle has a small body.
// @param candleRange Candlestick range (high - low).
// @returns [bool detected, string name, string type, string description].
export detectOnNeckBearish(bool downTrend, bool blackBody, bool longBody, bool whiteBody, float p_open, float p_close, float p_low, float bodyAvg, bool smallBody, float candleRange) =>
    C_OnNeckBearish = downTrend and blackBody[1] and longBody[1] and whiteBody and p_open < p_close[1] and smallBody and candleRange != 0 and math.abs(p_close - p_low[1]) <= bodyAvg * 0.05
    [C_OnNeckBearish, "On Neck", "Bearish", "On Neck is a two-line continuation pattern found in a downtrend. The first candle is long and red, the second candle is short and has a green body. The closing price of the second candle is close or equal to the first candle's low price. The pattern hints at a continuation of a downtrend, and penetrating the low of the green candlestick is sometimes considered a confirmation."]

// Pattern: Rising Window (Bullish)
export detectRisingWindowBullish(bool upTrend, float p_low, float p_high, float candleRange) =>
    C_RisingWindowBullish = upTrend[1] and (candleRange != 0 and candleRange[1] != 0) and p_low > p_high[1]
    [C_RisingWindowBullish, "Rising Window", "Bullish", "Rising Window is a two-candle bullish continuation pattern that forms during an uptrend. Both candles in the pattern can be of any type with the exception of the Four-Price Doji. The most important characteristic of the pattern is a price gap between the first candle's high and the second candle's low. That gap (window) between two bars signifies support against the selling pressure."]

// Pattern: Falling Window (Bearish)
export detectFallingWindowBearish(bool downTrend, float p_high, float p_low, float candleRange) =>
    C_FallingWindowBearish = downTrend[1] and (candleRange != 0 and candleRange[1] != 0) and p_high < p_low[1]
    [C_FallingWindowBearish, "Falling Window", "Bearish", "Falling Window is a two-candle bearish continuation pattern that forms during a downtrend. Both candles in the pattern can be of any type, with the exception of the Four-Price Doji. The most important characteristic of the pattern is a price gap between the first candle's low and the second candle's high. The existence of this gap (window) means that the bearish trend is expected to continue."]

// Pattern: Falling Three Methods (Bearish)
export detectFallingThreeMethodsBearish(bool downTrend, bool longBody, bool blackBody, bool smallBody, bool whiteBody, float p_open, float p_close, float p_low, float p_high) =>
    C_FallingThreeMethodsBearish = downTrend[4] and (longBody[4] and blackBody[4]) and (smallBody[3] and whiteBody[3] and p_open[3] > p_low[4] and p_close[3] < p_high[4]) and (smallBody[2] and whiteBody[2] and p_open[2] > p_low[4] and p_close[2] < p_high[4]) and (smallBody[1] and whiteBody[1] and p_open[1] > p_low[4] and p_close[1] < p_high[4]) and (longBody and blackBody and p_close < p_close[4])
    [C_FallingThreeMethodsBearish, "Falling Three Methods", "Bearish", "Falling Three Methods is a five-candle bearish pattern that signifies a continuation of an existing downtrend. The first candle is long and red, followed by three short green candles with bodies inside the range of the first candle. The last candle is also red and long and it closes below the close of the first candle. This decisive fifth strongly bearish candle hints that bulls could not reverse the prior downtrend and that bears have regained control of the market."]

// Pattern: Rising Three Methods (Bullish)
export detectRisingThreeMethodsBullish(bool upTrend, bool longBody, bool whiteBody, bool smallBody, bool blackBody, float p_open, float p_close, float p_low, float p_high) =>
    C_RisingThreeMethodsBullish = upTrend[4] and (longBody[4] and whiteBody[4]) and (smallBody[3] and blackBody[3] and p_open[3] < p_high[4] and p_close[3] > p_low[4]) and (smallBody[2] and blackBody[2] and p_open[2] < p_high[4] and p_close[2] > p_low[4]) and (smallBody[1] and blackBody[1] and p_open[1] < p_high[4] and p_close[1] > p_low[4]) and (longBody and whiteBody and p_close > p_close[4])
    [C_RisingThreeMethodsBullish, "Rising Three Methods", "Bullish", "Rising Three Methods is a five-candle bullish pattern that signifies a continuation of an existing uptrend. The first candle is long and green, followed by three short red candles with bodies inside the range of the first candle. The last candle is also green and long and it closes above the close of the first candle. This decisive fifth strongly bullish candle hints that bears could not reverse the prior uptrend and that bulls have regained control of the market."]

// Pattern: Tweezer Top (Bearish)
export detectTweezerTopBearish(bool upTrend, bool isDojiBody, bool hasUpShadow, bool hasDnShadow, float p_high, float bodyAvg, bool whiteBody, bool blackBody, bool longBody) =>
    C_TweezerTopBearish = upTrend[1] and (not isDojiBody or (hasUpShadow and hasDnShadow)) and math.abs(p_high - p_high[1]) <= bodyAvg * 0.05 and whiteBody[1] and blackBody and longBody[1]
    [C_TweezerTopBearish, "Tweezer Top", "Bearish", "Tweezer Top is a two-candle pattern that signifies a potential bearish reversal. The pattern is found during an uptrend. The first candle is long and green, the second candle is red, and its high is nearly identical to the high of the previous candle. The virtually identical highs, together with the inverted directions, hint that bears might be taking over the market."]

// Pattern: Tweezer Bottom (Bullish)
export detectTweezerBottomBullish(bool downTrend, bool isDojiBody, bool hasUpShadow, bool hasDnShadow, float p_low, float bodyAvg, bool blackBody, bool whiteBody, bool longBody) =>
    C_TweezerBottomBullish = downTrend[1] and (not isDojiBody or (hasUpShadow and hasDnShadow)) and math.abs(p_low - p_low[1]) <= bodyAvg * 0.05 and blackBody[1] and whiteBody and longBody[1]
    [C_TweezerBottomBullish, "Tweezer Bottom", "Bullish", "Tweezer Bottom is a two-candle pattern that signifies a potential bullish reversal. The pattern is found during a downtrend. The first candle is long and red, the second candle is green, its lows nearly identical to the low of the previous candle. The virtually identical lows together with the inverted directions hint that bulls might be taking over the market."]

// Pattern: Dark Cloud Cover (Bearish)
export detectDarkCloudCoverBearish(bool upTrend, bool whiteBody, bool longBody, bool blackBody, float p_open, float p_high, float p_close, float bodyMiddle) =>
    C_DarkCloudCoverBearish = (upTrend[1] and whiteBody[1] and longBody[1]) and (blackBody and p_open >= p_high[1] and p_close < bodyMiddle[1] and p_close > p_open[1])
    [C_DarkCloudCoverBearish, "Dark Cloud Cover", "Bearish", "Dark Cloud Cover is a two-candle bearish reversal candlestick pattern found in an uptrend. The first candle is green and has a larger than average body. The second candle is red and opens above the high of the prior candle, creating a gap, and then closes below the midpoint of the first candle. The pattern shows a possible shift in the momentum from the upside to the downside, indicating that a reversal might happen soon."]

// Pattern: Downside Tasuki Gap (Bearish)
export detectDownsideTasukiGapBearish(bool longBody, bool smallBody, bool downTrend, bool blackBody, bool whiteBody, float bodyHi, float bodyLo) =>
    C_DownsideTasukiGapBearish = longBody[2] and smallBody[1] and downTrend and blackBody[2] and bodyHi[1] < bodyLo[2] and blackBody[1] and whiteBody and bodyHi <= bodyLo[2] and bodyHi >= bodyHi[1]
    [C_DownsideTasukiGapBearish, "Downside Tasuki Gap", "Bearish", "Downside Tasuki Gap is a three-candle pattern found in a downtrend that usually hints at the continuation of the downtrend. The first candle is long and red, followed by a smaller red candle with its opening price that gaps below the body of the previous candle. The third candle is green and it closes inside the gap created by the first two candles, unable to close it fully. The bull’s inability to close that gap hints that the downtrend might continue."]

// Pattern: Upside Tasuki Gap (Bullish)
export detectUpsideTasukiGapBullish(bool longBody, bool smallBody, bool upTrend, bool whiteBody, bool blackBody, float bodyLo, float bodyHi) =>
    C_UpsideTasukiGapBullish = longBody[2] and smallBody[1] and upTrend and whiteBody[2] and bodyLo[1] > bodyHi[2] and whiteBody[1] and blackBody and bodyLo >= bodyHi[2] and bodyLo <= bodyLo[1]
    [C_UpsideTasukiGapBullish, "Upside Tasuki Gap", "Bullish", "Upside Tasuki Gap is a three-candle pattern found in an uptrend that usually hints at the continuation of the uptrend. The first candle is long and green, followed by a smaller green candle with its opening price that gaps above the body of the previous candle. The third candle is red and it closes inside the gap created by the first two candles, unable to close it fully. The bear’s inability to close the gap hints that the uptrend might continue."]

// Pattern: Evening Doji Star (Bearish)
export detectEveningDojiStarBearish(bool longBody, bool isDojiBody, bool upTrend, bool whiteBody, bool blackBody, float bodyLo, float bodyHi, float bodyMiddle) =>
    C_EveningDojiStarBearish = longBody[2] and isDojiBody[1] and longBody and upTrend and whiteBody[2] and bodyLo[1] > bodyHi[2] and blackBody and bodyLo <= bodyMiddle[2] and bodyLo > bodyLo[2] and bodyLo[1] > bodyHi
    [C_EveningDojiStarBearish, "Evening Doji Star", "Bearish", "This candlestick pattern is a variation of the Evening Star pattern. It is bearish and continues an uptrend with a long-bodied, green candle day. It is then followed by a gap and a Doji candle and concludes with a downward close. The close would be below the first day’s midpoint. It is more bearish than the regular evening star pattern because of the existence of the Doji."]

// Pattern: Doji Star (Bearish)
export detectDojiStarBearish(bool upTrend, bool whiteBody, bool longBody, bool isDojiBody, float bodyLo, float bodyHi) =>
    C_DojiStarBearish = upTrend and whiteBody[1] and longBody[1] and isDojiBody and bodyLo > bodyHi[1]
    [C_DojiStarBearish, "Doji Star", "Bearish", "This is a bearish reversal candlestick pattern that is found in an uptrend and consists of two candles. First comes a long green candle, followed by a Doji candle (except 4-Price Doji) that opens above the body of the first one, creating a gap. It is considered a reversal signal with confirmation during the next trading day."]

// Pattern: Doji Star (Bullish)
export detectDojiStarBullish(bool downTrend, bool blackBody, bool longBody, bool isDojiBody, float bodyHi, float bodyLo) =>
    C_DojiStarBullish = downTrend and blackBody[1] and longBody[1] and isDojiBody and bodyHi < bodyLo[1]
    [C_DojiStarBullish, "Doji Star", "Bullish", "This is a bullish reversal candlestick pattern that is found in a downtrend and consists of two candles. First comes a long red candle, followed by a Doji candle (except 4-Price Doji) that opens below the body of the first one, creating a gap. It is considered a reversal signal with confirmation during the next trading day."]

// Pattern: Morning Doji Star (Bullish)
export detectMorningDojiStarBullish(bool longBody, bool isDojiBody, bool downTrend, bool blackBody, bool whiteBody, float bodyHi, float bodyLo, float bodyMiddle) =>
    C_MorningDojiStarBullish = longBody[2] and isDojiBody[1] and longBody and downTrend and blackBody[2] and bodyHi[1] < bodyLo[2] and whiteBody and bodyHi >= bodyMiddle[2] and bodyHi < bodyHi[2] and bodyHi[1] < bodyLo
    [C_MorningDojiStarBullish, "Morning Doji Star", "Bullish", "This candlestick pattern is a variation of the Morning Star pattern. A three-day bullish reversal pattern, which consists of three candlesticks will look something like this: The first being a long-bodied red candle that extends the current downtrend. Next comes a Doji that gaps down on the open. After that comes a long-bodied green candle, which gaps up on the open and closes above the midpoint of the body of the first day. It is more bullish than the regular morning star pattern because of the existence of the Doji."]

// Pattern: Piercing (Bullish)
export detectPiercingBullish(bool downTrend, bool blackBody, bool longBody, bool whiteBody, float p_open, float p_low, float p_close, float bodyMiddle) =>
    C_PiercingBullish = (downTrend[1] and blackBody[1] and longBody[1]) and (whiteBody and p_open <= p_low[1] and p_close > bodyMiddle[1] and p_close < p_open[1])
    [C_PiercingBullish, "Piercing", "Bullish", "Piercing is a two-candle bullish reversal candlestick pattern found in a downtrend. The first candle is red and has a larger than average body. The second candle is green and opens below the low of the prior candle, creating a gap, and then closes above the midpoint of the first candle. The pattern shows a possible shift in the momentum from the downside to the upside, indicating that a reversal might happen soon."]

// Pattern: Hammer (Bullish)
export detectHammerBullish(bool smallBody, float body, float bodyLo, float p_hl2, float dnShadow, float factor, bool hasUpShadow, bool downTrend) =>
    C_HammerBullish = smallBody and body > 0 and bodyLo > p_hl2 and dnShadow >= factor * body and not hasUpShadow and downTrend
    [C_HammerBullish, "Hammer", "Bullish", "Hammer candlesticks form when a security moves lower after the open, but continues to rally into close above the intraday low. The candlestick that you are left with will look like a square attached to a long stick-like figure. This candlestick is called a Hammer if it happens to form during a decline."]

// Pattern: Hanging Man (Bearish)
export detectHangingManBearish(bool smallBody, float body, float bodyLo, float p_hl2, float dnShadow, float factor, bool hasUpShadow, bool upTrend) =>
    C_HangingManBearish = smallBody and body > 0 and bodyLo > p_hl2 and dnShadow >= factor * body and not hasUpShadow and upTrend
    [C_HangingManBearish, "Hanging Man", "Bearish", "When a specified security notably moves lower after the open, but continues to rally to close above the intraday low, a Hanging Man candlestick will form. The candlestick will resemble a square, attached to a long stick-like figure. It is referred to as a Hanging Man if the candlestick forms during an advance."]

// Pattern: Shooting Star (Bearish)
export detectShootingStarBearish(bool smallBody, float body, float bodyHi, float p_hl2, float upShadow, float factor, bool hasDnShadow, bool upTrend) =>
    C_ShootingStarBearish = smallBody and body > 0 and bodyHi < p_hl2 and upShadow >= factor * body and not hasDnShadow and upTrend
    [C_ShootingStarBearish, "Shooting Star", "Bearish", "This single day pattern can appear during an uptrend and opens high, while it closes near its open. It trades much higher as well. It is bearish in nature, but looks like an Inverted Hammer."]

// Pattern: Inverted Hammer (Bullish)
export detectInvertedHammerBullish(bool smallBody, float body, float bodyHi, float p_hl2, float upShadow, float factor, bool hasDnShadow, bool downTrend) =>
    C_InvertedHammerBullish = smallBody and body > 0 and bodyHi < p_hl2 and upShadow >= factor * body and not hasDnShadow and downTrend
    [C_InvertedHammerBullish, "Inverted Hammer", "Bullish", "If in a downtrend, then the open is lower. When it eventually trades higher, but closes near its open, it will look like an inverted version of the Hammer Candlestick. This is a one-day bullish reversal pattern."]

// Pattern: Morning Star (Bullish)
export detectMorningStarBullish(bool longBody, bool smallBody, bool downTrend, bool blackBody, bool whiteBody, float bodyHi, float bodyLo, float bodyMiddle) =>
    C_MorningStarBullish = longBody[2] and smallBody[1] and longBody and downTrend and blackBody[2] and bodyHi[1] < bodyLo[2] and whiteBody and bodyHi >= bodyMiddle[2] and bodyHi < bodyHi[2] and bodyHi[1] < bodyLo
    [C_MorningStarBullish, "Morning Star", "Bullish", "A three-day bullish reversal pattern, which consists of three candlesticks will look something like this: The first being a long-bodied red candle that extends the current downtrend. Next comes a short, middle candle that gaps down on the open. After comes a long-bodied green candle, which gaps up on the open and closes above the midpoint of the body of the first day."]

// Pattern: Evening Star (Bearish)
export detectEveningStarBearish(bool longBody, bool smallBody, bool upTrend, bool whiteBody, bool blackBody, float bodyLo, float bodyHi, float bodyMiddle) =>
    C_EveningStarBearish = longBody[2] and smallBody[1] and longBody and upTrend and whiteBody[2] and bodyLo[1] > bodyHi[2] and blackBody and bodyLo <= bodyMiddle[2] and bodyLo > bodyLo[2] and bodyLo[1] > bodyHi
    [C_EveningStarBearish, "Evening Star", "Bearish", "This candlestick pattern is bearish and continues an uptrend with a long-bodied, green candle day. It is then followed by a gapped and small-bodied candle day, and concludes with a downward close. The close would be below the first day’s midpoint."]

// Pattern: Marubozu White (Bullish)
export detectMarubozuWhiteBullish(bool whiteBody, bool longBody, float upShadow, float dnShadow, float body) =>
    C_MarubozuShadowPercentWhite = 5.0
    C_MarubozuWhiteBullish = whiteBody and longBody and upShadow <= C_MarubozuShadowPercentWhite / 100 * body and dnShadow <= C_MarubozuShadowPercentWhite / 100 * body
    [C_MarubozuWhiteBullish, "Marubozu White", "Bullish", "A Marubozu White Candle is a candlestick that does not have a shadow that extends from its candle body at either the open or the close. Marubozu is Japanese for 'close-cropped' or 'close-cut.' Other sources may call it a Bald or Shaven Head Candle."]

// Pattern: Marubozu Black (Bearish)
export detectMarubozuBlackBearish(bool blackBody, bool longBody, float upShadow, float dnShadow, float body) =>
    C_MarubozuShadowPercentBearish = 5.0
    C_MarubozuBlackBearish = blackBody and longBody and upShadow <= C_MarubozuShadowPercentBearish / 100 * body and dnShadow <= C_MarubozuShadowPercentBearish / 100 * body
    [C_MarubozuBlackBearish, "Marubozu Black", "Bearish", "This is a candlestick that has no shadow, which extends from the red-bodied candle at the open, the close, or even at both. In Japanese, the name means 'close-cropped' or 'close-cut.' The candlestick can also be referred to as Bald or Shaven Head."]

// Pattern: Doji
export detectDoji(bool doji, bool isDojiBody, float upShadow, float dnShadow, float body) =>
    C_DragonflyDoji = isDojiBody and upShadow <= body
    C_GravestoneDojiOne = isDojiBody and dnShadow <= body
    C_Doji = doji and not C_DragonflyDoji and not C_GravestoneDojiOne
    [C_Doji, "Doji", "Neutral", "When the open and close of a security are essentially equal to each other, a doji candle forms. The length of both upper and lower shadows may vary, causing the candlestick you are left with to either resemble a cross, an inverted cross, or a plus sign. Doji candles show the playout of buyer-seller indecision in a tug-of-war of sorts. As price moves either above or below the opening level during the session, the close is either at or near the opening level."]

// Pattern: Gravestone Doji (Bearish)
export detectGravestoneDojiBearish(bool isDojiBody, float dnShadow, float body) =>
    C_GravestoneDojiBearish = isDojiBody and dnShadow <= body
    [C_GravestoneDojiBearish, "Gravestone Doji", "Bearish", "When a doji is at or is close to the day’s low point, a doji line will develop."]

// Pattern: Dragonfly Doji (Bullish)
export detectDragonflyDojiBullish(bool isDojiBody, float upShadow, float body) =>
    C_DragonflyDojiBullish = isDojiBody and upShadow <= body
    [C_DragonflyDojiBullish, "Dragonfly Doji", "Bullish", "Similar to other Doji days, this particular Doji also regularly appears at pivotal market moments. This is a specific Doji where both the open and close price are at the high of a given day."]

// Pattern: Harami Cross (Bullish)
export detectHaramiCrossBullish(bool longBody, bool blackBody, bool downTrend, bool isDojiBody, float p_high, float p_low, float bodyHi, float bodyLo) =>
    C_HaramiCrossBullish = longBody[1] and blackBody[1] and downTrend[1] and isDojiBody and p_high <= bodyHi[1] and p_low >= bodyLo[1]
    [C_HaramiCrossBullish, "Harami Cross", "Bullish", "This candlestick pattern is a variation of the Harami Bullish pattern. It is found during a downtrend. The two-day candlestick pattern consists of a Doji candle that is entirely encompassed within the body of what was once a red-bodied candle."]

// Pattern: Harami Cross (Bearish)
export detectHaramiCrossBearish(bool longBody, bool whiteBody, bool upTrend, bool isDojiBody, float p_high, float p_low, float bodyHi, float bodyLo) =>
    C_HaramiCrossBearish = longBody[1] and whiteBody[1] and upTrend[1] and isDojiBody and p_high <= bodyHi[1] and p_low >= bodyLo[1]
    [C_HaramiCrossBearish, "Harami Cross", "Bearish", "This candlestick pattern is a variation of the Harami Bearish pattern. It is found during an uptrend. This is a two-day candlestick pattern with a Doji candle that is entirely encompassed within the body that was once a green-bodied candle. The Doji shows that some indecision has entered the minds of sellers, and the pattern hints that the trend might reverse."]

// Pattern: Harami (Bullish)
export detectHaramiBullish(bool longBody, bool blackBody, bool downTrend, bool whiteBody, bool smallBody, float p_high, float p_low, float bodyHi, float bodyLo) =>
    C_HaramiBullish = longBody[1] and blackBody[1] and downTrend[1] and whiteBody and smallBody and p_high <= bodyHi[1] and p_low >= bodyLo[1]
    [C_HaramiBullish, "Harami", "Bullish", "This two-day candlestick pattern consists of a small-bodied green candle that is entirely encompassed within the body of what was once a red-bodied candle."]

// Pattern: Harami (Bearish)
export detectHaramiBearish(bool longBody, bool whiteBody, bool upTrend, bool blackBody, bool smallBody, float p_high, float p_low, float bodyHi, float bodyLo) =>
    C_HaramiBearish = longBody[1] and whiteBody[1] and upTrend[1] and blackBody and smallBody and p_high <= bodyHi[1] and p_low >= bodyLo[1]
    [C_HaramiBearish, "Harami", "Bearish", "This is a two-day candlestick pattern with a small, red-bodied candle that is entirely encompassed within the body that was once a green-bodied candle."]

// Pattern: Long Lower Shadow (Bullish)
export detectLongLowerShadowBullish(float dnShadow, float candleRange) =>
    C_LongLowerShadowPercent = 75.0
    C_LongLowerShadowBullish = dnShadow > candleRange / 100 * C_LongLowerShadowPercent
    [C_LongLowerShadowBullish, "Long Lower Shadow", "Bullish", "To indicate seller domination of the first part of a session, candlesticks will present with long lower shadows and short upper shadows, consequently lowering prices."]

// Pattern: Long Upper Shadow (Bearish)
export detectLongUpperShadowBearish(float upShadow, float candleRange) =>
    C_LongShadowPercent = 75.0
    C_LongUpperShadowBearish = upShadow > candleRange / 100 * C_LongShadowPercent
    [C_LongUpperShadowBearish, "Long Upper Shadow", "Bearish", "To indicate buyer domination of the first part of a session, candlesticks will present with long upper shadows, as well as short lower shadows, consequently raising bidding prices."]

// Pattern: Spinning Top White
export detectSpinningTopWhite(float dnShadow, float upShadow, float candleRange, bool isDojiBody, bool whiteBody) =>
    C_SpinningTopWhitePercent = 34.0
    C_IsSpinningTopWhite = dnShadow >= candleRange / 100 * C_SpinningTopWhitePercent and upShadow >= candleRange / 100 * C_SpinningTopWhitePercent and not isDojiBody
    C_SpinningTopWhite = C_IsSpinningTopWhite and whiteBody
    [C_SpinningTopWhite, "Spinning Top White", "Neutral", "White spinning tops are candlestick lines that are small, green-bodied, and possess shadows (upper and lower) that end up exceeding the length of candle bodies. They often signal indecision between buyer and seller."]

// Pattern: Spinning Top Black
export detectSpinningTopBlack(float dnShadow, float upShadow, float candleRange, bool isDojiBody, bool blackBody) =>
    C_SpinningTopBlackPercent = 34.0
    C_IsSpinningTop = dnShadow >= candleRange / 100 * C_SpinningTopBlackPercent and upShadow >= candleRange / 100 * C_SpinningTopBlackPercent and not isDojiBody
    C_SpinningTopBlack = C_IsSpinningTop and blackBody
    [C_SpinningTopBlack, "Spinning Top Black", "Neutral", "Black spinning tops are candlestick lines that are small, red-bodied, and possess shadows (upper and lower) that end up exceeding the length of candle bodies. They often signal indecision."]

// Pattern: Three White Soldiers (Bullish)
export detectThreeWhiteSoldiersBullish(bool longBody, bool whiteBody, float p_close, float p_open, float candleRange, float upShadow) =>
    C_3WSld_ShadowPercent = 5.0
    C_3WSld_HaveNotUpShadow = candleRange * C_3WSld_ShadowPercent / 100 > upShadow
    C_ThreeWhiteSoldiersBullish = longBody and longBody[1] and longBody[2] and whiteBody and whiteBody[1] and whiteBody[2] and p_close > p_close[1] and p_close[1] > p_close[2] and p_open < p_close[1] and p_open > p_open[1] and p_open[1] < p_close[2] and p_open[1] > p_open[2] and C_3WSld_HaveNotUpShadow and C_3WSld_HaveNotUpShadow[1] and C_3WSld_HaveNotUpShadow[2]
    [C_ThreeWhiteSoldiersBullish, "Three White Soldiers", "Bullish", "This bullish reversal pattern is made up of three long-bodied, green candles in immediate succession. Each one opens within the body before it and the close is near to the daily high."]

// Pattern: Three Black Crows (Bearish)
export detectThreeBlackCrowsBearish(bool longBody, bool blackBody, float p_close, float p_open, float candleRange, float dnShadow) =>
    C_3BCrw_ShadowPercent = 5.0
    C_3BCrw_HaveNotDnShadow = candleRange * C_3BCrw_ShadowPercent / 100 > dnShadow
    C_ThreeBlackCrowsBearish = longBody and longBody[1] and longBody[2] and blackBody and blackBody[1] and blackBody[2] and p_close < p_close[1] and p_close[1] < p_close[2] and p_open > p_close[1] and p_open < p_open[1] and p_open[1] > p_close[2] and p_open[1] < p_open[2] and C_3BCrw_HaveNotDnShadow and C_3BCrw_HaveNotDnShadow[1] and C_3BCrw_HaveNotDnShadow[2]
    [C_ThreeBlackCrowsBearish, "Three Black Crows", "Bearish", "This is a bearish reversal pattern that consists of three long, red-bodied candles in immediate succession. For each of these candles, each day opens within the body of the day before and closes either at or near its low."]

// Pattern: Engulfing (Bullish)
export detectEngulfingBullish(bool downTrend, bool whiteBody, bool longBody, bool blackBody, bool smallBody, float p_close, float p_open) =>
    C_EngulfingBullish = downTrend and whiteBody and longBody and blackBody[1] and smallBody[1] and p_close >= p_open[1] and p_open <= p_close[1] and (p_close > p_open[1] or p_open < p_close[1])
    [C_EngulfingBullish, "Engulfing", "Bullish", "At the end of a given downward trend, there will most likely be a reversal pattern. To distinguish the first day, this candlestick pattern uses a small body, followed by a day where the candle body fully overtakes the body from the day before, and closes in the trend’s opposite direction. Although similar to the outside reversal chart pattern, it is not essential for this pattern to completely overtake the range (high to low), rather only the open and the close."]

// Pattern: Engulfing (Bearish)
export detectEngulfingBearish(bool upTrend, bool blackBody, bool longBody, bool whiteBody, bool smallBody, float p_close, float p_open) =>
    C_EngulfingBearish = upTrend and blackBody and longBody and whiteBody[1] and smallBody[1] and p_close <= p_open[1] and p_open >= p_close[1] and (p_close < p_open[1] or p_open > p_close[1])
    [C_EngulfingBearish, "Engulfing", "Bearish", "At the end of a given uptrend, a reversal pattern will most likely appear. During the first day, this candlestick pattern uses a small body. It is then followed by a day where the candle body fully overtakes the body from the day before it and closes in the trend’s opposite direction. Although similar to the outside reversal chart pattern, it is not essential for this pattern to fully overtake the range (high to low), rather only the open and the close."]

// Pattern: Abandoned Baby (Bullish)
export detectAbandonedBabyBullish(bool downTrend, bool blackBody, bool whiteBody, float p_low, float p_high, bool isDojiBody) =>
    C_AbandonedBabyBullish = downTrend[2] and blackBody[2] and isDojiBody[1] and p_low[2] > p_high[1] and whiteBody and p_high[1] < p_low
    [C_AbandonedBabyBullish, "Abandoned Baby", "Bullish", "This candlestick pattern is quite rare as far as reversal patterns go. The first of the pattern is a large down candle. Next comes a doji candle that gaps below the candle before it. The doji candle is then followed by another candle that opens even higher and swiftly moves to the upside."]

// Pattern: Abandoned Baby (Bearish)
export detectAbandonedBabyBearish(bool upTrend, bool whiteBody, bool blackBody, float p_high, float p_low, bool isDojiBody) =>
    C_AbandonedBabyBearish = upTrend[2] and whiteBody[2] and isDojiBody[1] and p_high[2] < p_low[1] and blackBody and p_low[1] > p_high
    [C_AbandonedBabyBearish, "Abandoned Baby", "Bearish", "A bearish abandoned baby is a specific candlestick pattern that often signals a downward reversal trend in terms of security price. It is formed when a gap appears between the lowest price of a doji-like candle and the candlestick of the day before. The earlier candlestick is green, tall, and has small shadows. The doji candle is also tailed by a gap between its lowest price point and the highest price point of the candle that comes next, which is red, tall and also has small shadows. The doji candle shadows must completely gap either below or above the shadows of the first and third day in order to have the abandoned baby pattern effect."]

// Pattern: Tri-Star (Bullish)
export detectTriStarBullish(bool doji, bool downTrend, float bodyHi, float bodyLo) =>
    C_3DojisBullish = doji[2] and doji[1] and doji
    C_BodyGapUpBullish = bodyHi[1] < bodyLo
    C_BodyGapDnBullish = bodyLo[1] > bodyHi
    C_TriStarBullish = C_3DojisBullish and downTrend[2] and C_BodyGapDnBullish[1] and C_BodyGapUpBullish
    [C_TriStarBullish, "Tri-Star", "Bullish", "A bullish TriStar candlestick pattern can form when three doji candlesticks materialize in immediate succession at the tail-end of an extended downtrend. The first doji candle marks indecision between bull and bear. The second doji gaps in the direction of the leading trend. The third changes the attitude of the market once the candlestick opens in the direction opposite to the trend. Each doji candle has a shadow, all comparatively shallow, which signify an interim cutback in volatility."]

// Pattern: Tri-Star (Bearish)
export detectTriStarBearish(bool doji, bool upTrend, float bodyHi, float bodyLo) =>
    C_3Dojis = doji[2] and doji[1] and doji
    C_BodyGapUp = bodyHi[1] < bodyLo
    C_BodyGapDn = bodyLo[1] > bodyHi
    C_TriStarBearish = C_3Dojis and upTrend[2] and C_BodyGapUp[1] and C_BodyGapDn
    [C_TriStarBearish, "Tri-Star", "Bearish", "This particular pattern can form when three doji candlesticks appear in immediate succession at the end of an extended uptrend. The first doji candle marks indecision between bull and bear. The second doji gaps in the direction of the leading trend. The third changes the attitude of the market once the candlestick opens in the direction opposite to the trend. Each doji candle has a shadow, all comparatively shallow, which signify an interim cutback in volatility."]

// Pattern: Kicking (Bullish)
export detectKickingBullish(bool longBody, float upShadow, float dnShadow, float body, bool whiteBody, bool blackBody, float p_high, float p_low) =>
    C_MarubozuShadowPercent = 5.0
    C_Marubozu = longBody and upShadow <= C_MarubozuShadowPercent / 100 * body and dnShadow <= C_MarubozuShadowPercent / 100 * body
    C_MarubozuWhiteBullishKicking = C_Marubozu and whiteBody
    C_MarubozuBlackBullish = C_Marubozu and blackBody
    C_KickingBullish = C_MarubozuBlackBullish[1] and C_MarubozuWhiteBullishKicking and p_high[1] < p_low
    [C_KickingBullish, "Kicking", "Bullish", "The first day candlestick is a bearish marubozu candlestick with next to no upper or lower shadow and where the price opens at the day’s high and closes at the day’s low. The second day is a bullish marubozu pattern, with next to no upper or lower shadow and where the price opens at the day’s low and closes at the day’s high. Additionally, the second day gaps up extensively and opens above the opening price of the day before. This gap or window, as the Japanese call it, lies between day one and day two’s bullish candlesticks."]

// Pattern: Kicking (Bearish)
export detectKickingBearish(bool longBody, float upShadow, float dnShadow, float body, bool whiteBody, bool blackBody, float p_low, float p_high) =>
    C_MarubozuBullishShadowPercent = 5.0
    C_MarubozuBearishKicking = longBody and upShadow <= C_MarubozuBullishShadowPercent / 100 * body and dnShadow <= C_MarubozuBullishShadowPercent / 100 * body
    C_MarubozuWhiteBearish = C_MarubozuBearishKicking and whiteBody
    C_MarubozuBlackBearishKicking = C_MarubozuBearishKicking and blackBody
    C_KickingBearish = C_MarubozuWhiteBearish[1] and C_MarubozuBlackBearishKicking and p_low[1] > p_high
    [C_KickingBearish, "Kicking", "Bearish", "A bearish kicking pattern will occur, subsequently signaling a reversal for a new downtrend. The first day candlestick is a bullish marubozu. The second day gaps down extensively and opens below the opening price of the day before. There is a gap between day one and two’s bearish candlesticks."]